WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.880
Peter Parker is getting some slick new duds
in Spider-Man's second solo outing in the

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.180
Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.690
In December 2018, Brazil's Comic Con Experience
played host to a splashy rollout for the Homecoming

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.220
follow-up.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.760
One of the most exciting surprises was a new
black Spider-suit, built for stealth, which

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.400
we'll get to see in action when Spider-Man:
Far From Home sees release in July 2019.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.180
This won't be the first time we've gotten
to see Peter Parker rock an upgraded outfit

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.000
in the MCU.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.779
In Spider-Man: Homecoming, the first standalone
feature for Tom Holland's version of the wall-crawler,

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:35.640
the burgeoning hero initially wore a low-fi
homemade suit before slipping into the high-tech

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.480
outfit Tony Stark designed for him.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:43.340
At the time, that suit was the most technologically-advanced
outfit we'd ever seen Spider-Man wear onscreen,

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.920
with flash and flair and an AI assistant to
rival Iron Man's armor.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:51.560
"Hey suit lady, I kind of feel bad calling
you suit lady, you know?

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.580
I think I should probably give you a name."

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.879
But while Tony Stark played a big part in
Spider-Man: Homecoming, it doesn't look as

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.580
though the character will be appearing at
all in Far From Home.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:06.320
The absence of Iron Man has led some fans
to conclude that Avengers: Endgame will mark

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.420
Mr. Stark's swan song, but we're not too sure
about that yet.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.540
A lot needs to be explained in the MCU's story
between now and Far From Home's release, like

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.580
how exactly Peter is going to be coming back
to life.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.640
To be honest, this whole movie should come
with a spoiler alert.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.980
Instead of an assist from Stark Industries,
it looks like Far From Home will instead feature

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:29.509
Peter getting some help from former S.H.I.E.L.D.
agents Maria Hill and Nick Fury, and considering

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:33.549
their super-spy bona fides, they may well
have had a hand in getting Peter his sleek

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:34.540
new stealth suit.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:39.170
In stark contrast to the ultra-high-tech Iron
Spider suit featured in Avengers: Infinity

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:42.840
War, the stealth suit features a decidedly
more low-tech aesthetic.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:47.400
Blurry photos of the new suit have been circulating
around the internet since Far From Home started

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.600
filming, but now we've got the first official
look at the new duds.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.130
The photo shows Spider-Man star Tom Holland
suited up in the sleek costume, perched on

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.770
what looks like the edge of a window.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:01.810
The new black suit has almost no resemblance
to the classic black symbiote suit, and it's

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:05.620
also much more low-tech than the stealth suit
from the Spider-Man PS4 game.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.940
This take on the stealth suit looks to be
composed of a fine mesh underlayer, with several

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.140
tactical accessories.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:15.780
There's a flak jacket-like chest piece, complete
with a visible zipper, and eyepieces in the

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.040
classic Spidey shape.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.500
It also features thigh pads, shin-high boots,
fingerless gloves, and spiffy black web-shooters.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:26.260
In an interesting turnaround from the Iron
Spider suit, this getup actually looks like

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:29.930
something a well-funded teenager could put
together for themselves, which should be a

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.020
boon for hopeful cosplay enthusiasts.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:36.200
Beyond the new black super suit, we don't
know a great deal about what's going to go

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.160
down in Far From Home.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.819
We know that a great deal of the story will
be taking place in Europe, far away from Spidey's

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.739
typical haunts of Queens and Manhattan, hence
the title.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:49.260
And we also know that Jake Gyllenhaal will
be taking on the young Avenger as the nefarious

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.000
trickster villain Mysterio.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.900
But beyond those broad ideas, very few actual
plot details have emerged about the movie,

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:00.340
meaning that it isn't clear what kind of sneaky
missions might necessitate the new threads.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.780
Will Spider-Man be sneaking into some secret
facility?

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.960
Or will he be slinging himself around European
vistas while in hiding from his enemies?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.160
For now, it's up in the air.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.120
While we don't know what the suit will be
for, exactly, the inspiration for the suit's

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.300
design seems clear.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.840
The stealth suit bears more than a passing
resemblance to the outfit worn by a character

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:22.200
named Spider-Man Noir, an alternate universe
version of Spider-Man who's appeared in both

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.120
the comic books and the Sony animated feature
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.620
But enough about the new black suit, what's
going on with Peter's default outfit?

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.090
In October 2018, Tom Holland showed off a
revamped version of his classic Homecoming

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.319
suit during an appearance on Jimmy Kimmel
Live.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.980
It's a fairly simple redesign, swapping out
the blue portions of the original suit for

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:41.480
black.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:46.519
The stealth version, on the other hand, is
like nothing we've ever seen Spidey wear onscreen

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.140
before, even the black symbiote suit from
Sam Raimi's Spider-Man 3.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.000
But while Spider-Man's outfit is going dark
again, we're pretty sure he'll be keeping

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.180
his sunny personality this time around.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.120
A dark and gritty Spider-Man?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.120
That sounds like the last thing audiences
want.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.860
"Activating instant kill."

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.970
"Oh no-no-no-no-no I don't wanna kill anybody."

